{
  "summary": "Moves the `getblocktemplate` block template cache from function-local static variables in the RPC handler into `BlockTemplateManager`. The cache's lifetime is bound to the node context rather than the process, raw `CBlockIndex*` pointers are replaced with hash lookups, synchronization under `cs_main` is formally annotated, and unit tests are added for template invalidation.",
  "problem": "Template caching in `getblocktemplate` previously used process-scoped static variables. This allowed cached `CBlockIndex*` pointers to outlive their owning `ChainstateManager` during unit tests, bypassed compile-time thread-safety checking for `cs_main`, and prevented unit testing of the caching and refresh logic.",
  "evidence": [
    "Addresses the 'Remove remaining global states' TODO in tracking issue #33758.",
    "PR description points out that 'cached CBlockIndex* can outlive its ChainstateManager (as in unit tests)' and 'can't be unit tested.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "The change is primarily a code movement from `rpc/mining.cpp` to `node/block_template_manager.cpp`, accompanied by unit tests in `test/miner_tests.cpp`.",
  "changed_since_previous": "No structural changes to the commits or implementation; references to follow-up PR #36357 were removed.",
  "card": "Moves the getblocktemplate RPC cache from function-local statics into BlockTemplateManager. This eliminates process-wide global state where dangling CBlockIndex pointers could outlive ChainstateManager in tests, adds Clang thread-safety annotations under cs_main, and adds unit test coverage for template caching and invalidation rules. The refactor advances the BlockTemplateManager tracking issue #33758.",
